Dr.P.Venkata Ramana

Dr.P.Venkata Ramana, Professor of Mechanical Engineering Mahatma Gandhi Institute of Technology (MGIT), Hyderabad has graduated in Mechanical Engineering from Kakatiya University, Warangal. He has to his credit two M.Tech.s, first in Industrial Metallurgy from NIT, Warangal and the second in Production Engineering from JNTU Hyderabad. He has completed Ph.D. in Mechanical Engineering with specialisation in Welding of Advanced Materials from JNTU Hyderabad. So far he has published 25 papers in International and National Journals and conferences. Prof. Ramana has 18 years experience in Teaching at MGIT and 2 years in Industry.

Dr.Ramana has received several awards such as Weldwell Speciality Award for Best Ph.D. Thesis, I.T.Mirchandani Memorial Research Award, H.D.Govindraj Memorial Research Award, D&H; Secheron Award, IWS Award and appreciation as Best Teacher by the management of MGIT.

Dr. Ramana is the Faculty Advisor of ISTE Students- Chapter - MGIT. He was the Convenor of ISTE AP State Students Convention -2013. He is also Hon. Secretary of Indian Institute of Welding (IIW), Hyderabad Branch.
